<div class="unit-details">
    <div class="grid-2-col">
        <div class="content-box step-card">
            <span class="step-pill">Step 1</span>
            <h2 class="content-title"><i class="fa-solid fa-layer-group"></i> Understand the Swipes</h2>

            <p>Each card has a <strong>scenario</strong> (the situation) and an <strong>action</strong> (what someone did). Read both sides, then swipe based on your judgement.</p>

            <div class="grid-2-col" style="margin-top: 1.25rem;">
                <div class="callout" style="background: #e8f5e9; border-left-color: #2e7d32;">
                    <h3 style="font-size: 1.05rem; color: var(--primary-color); margin: 0;">← Good & Use Your Name</h3>
                    <p>No need to hide who you are.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="callout" style="background: #fff3e0; border-left-color: #ef6c00;">
                    <h3 style="font-size: 1.05rem; color: var(--primary-color); margin: 0;">→ Good but Stay Anonymous</h3>
                    <p>Better to use a nickname.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="callout" style="background: #e3f2fd; border-left-color: #1565c0;">
                    <h3 style="font-size: 1.05rem; color: var(--primary-color); margin: 0;">↑ It Depends…</h3>
                    <p>This one is complicated.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="callout" style="background: #ffebee; border-left-color: #c62828;">
                    <h3 style="font-size: 1.05rem; color: var(--primary-color); margin: 0;">↓ Not OK Online</h3>
                    <p>This shouldn't happen.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="content-box step-card">
            <span class="step-pill">Step 2</span>
            <h2 class="content-title"><i class="fa-solid fa-play"></i> Play Swipe Scenarios</h2>

            <p>Your goal is to sort the cards by swiping them to the best category.</p>

            <ul class="checklist">
                <li>Read the scenario and action carefully.</li>
                <li>Swipe in the direction that matches your judgement.</li>
                <li>If you're unsure, use <strong>It Depends…</strong> and explain why later.</li>
            </ul>

            <div class="activity-toolbar no-print" style="margin: 1rem 0 0; justify-content: flex-start;">
                <a href="Online-behaviour.html" class="action-btn action-btn--primary">
                    <i class="fa-solid fa-layer-group"></i>
                    Launch activity
                </a>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="content-box step-card">
        <span class="step-pill">Step 3</span>
        <h2 class="content-title"><i class="fa-solid fa-book"></i> Exercise Book Tasks</h2>
        <p>After completing the game, write answers for the prompts below:</p>

        <ul class="custom-list" style="margin-bottom: 0;">
            <li><strong>From "Not OK Online":</strong> Choose one card and explain why this behaviour is never acceptable.</li>
            <li><strong>From "Good & Use Your Name":</strong> Choose one card and explain why being yourself is good in this situation.</li>
            <li><strong>From "Good but Stay Anonymous":</strong> Choose one card and explain why staying anonymous makes sense.</li>
            <li><strong>From "It Depends…":</strong> Choose 3–4 cards and explore what makes each one complicated.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="content-box step-card">
        <span class="step-pill">Step 4</span>
        <h2 class="content-title"><i class="fa-solid fa-pen-to-square"></i> Reflection</h2>

        <div class="callout">
            <h3 style="font-size: 1.05rem; color: var(--primary-color); margin: 0;"><strong>A.</strong> Adapting Your Behaviour</h3>
            <p>Think about your sorted cards. Why do people behave differently on different platforms?</p>
        </div>

        <div class="callout">
            <h3 style="font-size: 1.05rem; color: var(--primary-color); margin: 0;"><strong>B.</strong> Context Collapse</h3>
            <p>What happens when something you post for your friends is suddenly seen by teachers, parents, or strangers? How does this change things?</p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="callout">
        <h2 class="content-title"><i class="fa-solid fa-graduation-cap"></i> By the end of this task, you should be able to…</h2>
        <ul class="custom-list" style="margin-bottom: 0;">
            <li>Identify ways online behaviour changes across different platforms</li>
            <li>Explain how digital identity can evolve over time</li>
            <li>Recognise when behaviour needs to adapt for safety, privacy, or wellbeing</li>
            <li>Understand the concept of "context collapse" in online spaces</li>
        </ul>
    </div>
</div>
